+        'A permit to work is a written system for non-routine, high-risk work. Hot work: welding, grinding, cutting, anything that makes sparks or flame. A confined space: an enclosed space with a narrow way in, such as a tank or a manhole, where the air can turn deadly. Also work at height, opening pipes or vessels that held process fluids, and digging near cables.\n\nIt makes sure the hazards are known, the area is ready, and everyone knows who is in control.',
