+        'Handover and closing are where it goes wrong. At a shift change the permit is handed over in person. When the job is done, the holder hands it back, the issuer checks the area, and only then are isolations removed.\n\nOn Piper Alpha, an oil platform in the North Sea, 167 people died in 1988. A pump was restarted while its safety valve was off for maintenance, the opening closed only by a loose cover plate; the permit for that work had not been passed on at shift change.',
