+        'The classic safety number is the lost-time injury: an injury that keeps someone off work after the day it happened. It counts harm after the fact, and it can be gamed by moving injured people to light work.\n\nExperts argue for counting what prevents harm too: near misses reported, actions closed, serious risks fixed.\n\nA sharp question: “Which of our incidents last year could have killed someone, and what did we change after each one?”',
